### Quantum-Safe REST API — Example Requests
### Use with VS Code REST Client extension or convert to curl
### Base URL: http://localhost:8000

@base_url = http://localhost:8000
@token = PUT_TOKEN_HERE

# ============================================================
# 1. HEALTH CHECK
# ============================================================

### GET /  — API root health check
GET {{base_url}}/
Accept: application/json

###

# ============================================================
# 2. AUTHENTICATION
# ============================================================

### POST /api/register — Register a new user
POST {{base_url}}/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "alice_secure_pass123"
}

###

### POST /api/register — Register second user
POST {{base_url}}/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "bob_secure_pass123"
}

###

### POST /api/login — Login and get JWT token
# Copy the access_token from the response and set @token above
POST {{base_url}}/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "alice_secure_pass123"
}

###

### GET /api/me — Get current user info (requires auth)
GET {{base_url}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ============================================================
# 3. KEY MANAGEMENT
# ============================================================

### POST /api/keys/generate — Generate ML-KEM-768 + ML-DSA-65 key pairs
POST {{base_url}}/api/keys/generate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "algorithm": "both"
}

###

### POST /api/keys/generate — Generate only KEM keys
POST {{base_url}}/api/keys/generate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "algorithm": "kem"
}

###

### GET /api/keys/public — Get a user's public keys (no auth needed)
GET {{base_url}}/api/keys/public?username=alice
Accept: application/json

###

# ============================================================
# 4. KEY ENCAPSULATION MECHANISM (ML-KEM-768)
# ============================================================

### POST /api/kem/encapsulate — Alice encapsulates using Bob's public key
### Returns ciphertext + shared_secret_hash (never transmits the secret itself)
POST {{base_url}}/api/kem/encapsulate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "recipient_username": "bob"
}

###

### POST /api/kem/decapsulate — Bob decapsulates with his private key
### Replace kem_ciphertext with the value from /api/kem/encapsulate response
POST {{base_url}}/api/kem/decapsulate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "kem_ciphertext": "BASE64_CIPHERTEXT_FROM_ENCAPSULATE"
}

###

# ============================================================
# 5. ENCRYPTION / DECRYPTION (AES-256-GCM)
# ============================================================

### POST /api/encrypt — Encrypt a plaintext message for a recipient
POST {{base_url}}/api/encrypt
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "plaintext": "This is a quantum-safe encrypted message!",
  "recipient_username": "bob"
}

###

### POST /api/decrypt — Decrypt a ciphertext
### Replace field values with the response from /api/encrypt
POST {{base_url}}/api/decrypt
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "ciphertext": "BASE64_CIPHERTEXT",
  "nonce": "BASE64_NONCE",
  "kem_ciphertext": "BASE64_KEM_CIPHERTEXT"
}

###

# ============================================================
# 6. DIGITAL SIGNATURES (ML-DSA-65)
# ============================================================

### POST /api/sign — Sign a message with ML-DSA-65
POST {{base_url}}/api/sign
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "message": "I authorize this transaction. —Alice"
}

###

### POST /api/verify — Verify a digital signature (no auth needed)
### Replace signature with value from /api/sign response
POST {{base_url}}/api/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "signer_username": "alice",
  "message": "I authorize this transaction. —Alice",
  "signature": "BASE64_SIGNATURE"
}

###

### POST /api/verify — Demonstrate tamper detection (should return valid: false)
POST {{base_url}}/api/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "signer_username": "alice",
  "message": "I authorize this transaction. —Alice TAMPERED",
  "signature": "BASE64_SIGNATURE"
}

###

# ============================================================
# 7. SECURE MESSAGING
# ============================================================

### POST /api/messages/send — Send an encrypted + signed message
POST {{base_url}}/api/messages/send
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "recipient_username": "bob",
  "plaintext": "Hello Bob! This message is quantum-safe encrypted and signed."
}

###

### GET /api/messages — Get received messages (Bob's inbox)
GET {{base_url}}/api/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### GET /api/messages/{id} — Read and decrypt a specific message
### Replace 1 with actual message ID from /api/messages response
GET {{base_url}}/api/messages/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ============================================================
# 8. SECURITY & BENCHMARKING
# ============================================================

### GET /api/security/status — Get security configuration status
GET {{base_url}}/api/security/status
Accept: application/json

###

### GET /api/benchmark — Run PQC vs Classical crypto benchmark
### WARNING: This takes 30-120 seconds due to pure-Python PQC
GET {{base_url}}/api/benchmark
Accept: application/json

###

### GET /api/logs — Get cryptographic operation audit logs (requires auth)
GET {{base_url}}/api/logs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ============================================================
# SWAGGER UI
# ============================================================
# Interactive API documentation: http://localhost:8000/docs
# ReDoc documentation:          http://localhost:8000/redoc

